7. User Stories & Requirements
Epic Hypothesis
If we remove the backend server and route all data access through Supabase and Next.js server actions, then developers can ship features 50% faster and infrastructure costs drop significantly, without degrading the customer shopping experience.
User Stories
US-01 · Product Catalogue
As a customer, I want to browse all products with category filters so I can find what I want quickly.
●	Supabase query on products + categories tables, no backend intermediary
●	Supports pagination (≥ 12 products/page)
●	Images served from Supabase Storage public bucket 'product-images'

US-02 · Authentication
As a customer, I want to sign up / log in so my cart and order history are saved.
●	@supabase/ssr used for server-side session management in Next.js middleware
●	Session persists across page navigation (no re-login on refresh)
●	Supports email + password auth; Google OAuth optional (🔶 Assumption: not scoped yet)

US-03 · Cart & Checkout
As a customer, I want to add items to a cart and place an order with Razorpay payment.
●	Zustand manages cart state client-side
●	On checkout, a Next.js server action creates a Razorpay order and returns order_id
●	After payment, a server action verifies Razorpay signature and writes order to Supabase 'orders' table
●	Razorpay secret keys never exposed to client (serverExternalPackages config confirmed)

US-04 · WhatsApp Order Confirmation
As a customer, I want to receive an order confirmation via WhatsApp so I know my order was received.
●	Next.js server action (or webhook) calls WhatsApp Business API post-payment
●	Message contains order ID, items, total, and estimated dispatch time
●	🔵 Open Question: Use official WhatsApp Business API or Twilio WhatsApp gateway?

US-05 · Admin Order Management
As an admin, I want to view all orders and update their status from a protected dashboard.
●	Supabase RLS: admin role can read/write orders; customers can only read their own
●	Admin dashboard lists all orders with filter by status (pending / confirmed / dispatched)
●	Export to XLSX (xlsx library already in package.json)

US-06 · Security Headers
As the platform owner, I want all pages served with security headers to protect users.
●	next.config.ts already configures: Strict-Transport-Security, X-Frame-Options, CSP, Referrer-Policy
●	HTTPS enforced via Vercel / hosting provider

8. Out of Scope
●	Custom backend API server (Express, NestJS, Fastify) — this is explicitly removed
●	Mobile app (iOS / Android) — web-first only
●	Advanced search / Elasticsearch — basic Supabase full-text search sufficient for now
●	Inventory management system — manual stock updates via Supabase Studio
●	Multi-vendor marketplace — single-vendor (Asali Swad) only
●	Subscription / recurring payments — one-time purchases only for this phase
●	Google OAuth (🔵 Open Question — to be decided post-MVP)

9. Dependencies & Risks
Dependencies
●	Supabase project provisioned with correct RLS policies before go-live
●	Razorpay account configured with live keys and webhook URLs pointing to Next.js /api/razorpay/webhook
●	Vercel project connected to GitHub repo with env vars: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
●	WhatsApp Business API access or Twilio account (🔵 Open Question: provider choice)
Risks & Mitigations
Risk	Mitigation
Supabase RLS misconfiguration leaks customer data	Thorough RLS policy testing with separate admin and customer Supabase accounts before launch
Razorpay webhook replay attack	Verify HMAC signature on every webhook; reject duplicates using idempotency key stored in DB
Next.js server action timeout on slow Razorpay calls	Set max duration in vercel.json; add retry logic with exponential backoff
Supabase free-tier row limits hit unexpectedly	Monitor row counts; upgrade to Pro tier proactively (breakpoint: ~50k rows)
ngrok dev origin left in production config	Remove 'impromptu-trash-seizing.ngrok-free.dev' from allowedDevOrigins before production deploy


